    {
      "id": "claim_af534420566d4bc3b2709c57c8834678",
      "statement": "Active-tab fallback is the backward-compatibility invariant for tab targeting: when tabId is omitted or undefined, every layer (websocket-client targetEnvelope, background-controller extractTabId, page-reader helpers, and navigation adapters) falls back to the active foreground tab, so existing callers that omit tabId keep working unchanged. open_tab is intentionally exempt because it creates a new tab and returns its tabId.",
