    {
      "id": "claim_bd64511ce26c4e8bab9db8f16ee629c0",
      "statement": "The shared page-reader.ts helpers (readActiveTabPage, performActiveTabAction, performActiveTabBatch) are the convergence point for both browser adapters: they resolve a tab by numeric tabId when provided (using it directly as the sendMessage/executeScript target) or by querying the active tab when absent, re-inject content.js per ADR 0043, and map content-script responses into PageReadResult/PageActionResult/BatchResult. They do not call a tabs.get(tabId) validation because the TabsApi interface has no get member, so a stale or nonexistent tabId surfaces as a content-script/sendMessage failure rather than a dedicated tab-not-found error.",
      "evidence": [
